# ============================================================================
# TRAME PUBLIC HTTPS EDGE (Caddyfile)
# ============================================================================
#
# PURPOSE:
# --------
# The only container that publishes host ports (80/443). It obtains and renews
# a certificate for `TRAME_DOMAIN` automatically (ACME HTTP-01/TLS-ALPN-01, so
# ports 80 and 443 must be reachable from the internet) and redirects HTTP to
# HTTPS. `localhost` (local smoke test) gets a certificate from Caddy's
# internal CA instead.
#
# INVARIANTS & SAFETY BOUNDARIES:
# -------------------------------
#   1. `Single Proxy Hop`:
#      - No `trusted_proxies`: Caddy replaces any client `X-Forwarded-For`
#        with the socket peer, so `trame-server` runs with
#        `TRAME_TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS=1` and spoofed headers cannot pick a
#        rate-limit bucket.
#   2. Routes, compression and WebSocket rules: see `trame-routes.caddy`.
# ============================================================================

{$TRAME_DOMAIN} {
	import trame-routes.caddy
}
